WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.436 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:06.473
-JCPenney doesn't have aisles.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.774
They have, uh...

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:10.610
demilitarized zones.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.279
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:17.784
Maryland legalized marijuana,
and we made a joke.

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:21.454
The joke was, finally there was
something to do in Maryland.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:25.992
Well, Marylanders
responded in force.

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:30.062
I think they were just happy

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:31.898
to have something to do.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.970
I was told to visit Ocean City.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.306
I was told Maryland has
the best aquarium,

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:42.141
the best seafood spice rub,

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:44.811
and the best state flag.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.147
I looked up the state flag.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:49.649
This is the Maryland state flag.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:50.983
Pretty cool.

00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:54.153
So cool, I asked
if it wanted to hang out,

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:55.320
and it said it couldn't,

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.824
because it's too busy.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:01:00.026
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:09.401
We said the midterms were
less of a red wave

00:01:09.401 --> 00:01:11.237
and more of a Red Wedding,

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:14.240
if Donald Trump showed up
as a dragon

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.574
and burned it all to a crisp.

00:01:15.574 --> 00:01:17.410
A lot of Throners out there
told me that, you know,

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.413
there wasn't a dragon
at the Red Wedding.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.916
But if Donald Trump
was a dragon,

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:25.084
which he was in our analogy,

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:26.586
I think he would show up

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.588
whether or not
he was supposed to be there.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:31.924
This is a man who shows up to
weddings uninvited all the time.

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:33.593
We've established that
about him.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:36.429
[ Sighing ] Also, I try
to really hammer this home --

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:39.431
when I'm speaking as Trump,

00:01:39.431 --> 00:01:43.603
I would just invite you
not to correct errors there,

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:47.607
because I'm speaking
as Trump would.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.442
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:52.444
So, as Trump, I referred
to Frankenstein,

00:01:52.444 --> 00:01:54.780
and a lot of you said,

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.783
"Frankenstein's monster."

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.518
That would be so jarring

00:01:59.518 --> 00:02:02.188
if that was a detail
Donald Trump got right.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:05.024
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:09.862
This is a man who once referred
to Tim Cook, the CEO of Apple,

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:12.364
as Tim Apple.

00:02:12.364 --> 00:02:13.700
That's not a guy who says

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.703
[as Trump] Frankenstein's
monster, of course.

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.537
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:20.706
The correct way to say it.

00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:23.042
The great Mary Shelley.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:26.045
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:29.215
Married to Percy Bysshe Shelley,

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.549
my favorite of the Romantics.

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:32.719
I get romantic
just thinking about him.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:33.786
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.622
"Ozymandias" -- that's a poem.

00:02:36.622 --> 00:02:38.291
My favorite two lines --

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.793
"My name is Ozymandias,
king of kings --

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:43.862
Look on my works, ye Mighty,
and despair!"

00:02:43.862 --> 00:02:47.032
The only two lines
I've ever read of the poem.

00:02:47.032 --> 00:02:49.201
Pretty good message there.

00:02:49.201 --> 00:02:51.871
Put your name on stuff
and they'll never forget you.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.907
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:56.409
[Normal voice] Oh.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:03:01.915
We talked about
if Donald Trump

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:06.085
was on "American Ninja Warrior."

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:07.419
And I will say,
our graphics department

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:08.587
went above and beyond.

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:10.756
There was some confusion.

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:13.259
And we just wanted them to take
a cutout photo of Trump

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.593
and do this animation,
but they actually

00:03:14.593 --> 00:03:15.661
made it look like a video game.

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:17.163
It's wonderful.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:19.398
But some of you
had issues with it.

00:03:19.398 --> 00:03:20.899
Let's take a look,

00:03:20.899 --> 00:03:23.069
and then the rest of you
can guess while you're watching

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:24.737
what the issue was
from the jackals.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:25.738
Let's take a look.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.774
[ Video game sound effects ]

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:31.644
The criticism?

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.813
"He wouldn't make two!"

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.882
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:42.522
It's so hot.
Are you hot today in here?

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.659
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:47.993
Um, alright.

00:03:47.993 --> 00:03:50.997
So, we said we brought
a gopher in for a photo shoot,

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:52.498
but the gopher wouldn't
drink a beer

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:54.367
because he was a Mormon.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:58.503
That was an error of mine.

00:03:58.503 --> 00:03:59.505
He wasn't a Mormon --

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:01.340
he was a marmot.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.008
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.008 --> 00:04:06.345
And he did say it, but they
are hard to understand

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:08.013
'cause there's...

00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:10.549
when they talk, the gap
in their front teeth

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:12.385
makes like a whistling sound.

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:15.387
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.387 --> 00:04:18.724
Marmot, if you don't know,

00:04:18.724 --> 00:04:20.893
are large ground squirrels

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.229
who eat berries,
lichens, and moss,

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:25.231
but don't

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.600
drink alcohol, coffee, or tea.

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:31.371
It's not religious,
it's just like,

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:32.905
where are they gonna get it?

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.375
Speaking of that,

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:40.212
while discussing the gopher,
I was very unprofessional

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:41.380
last week during "Corrections."

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.381
I started laughing very hard.

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:43.883
I couldn't complete a sentence.

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:45.885
And that's not what
"Corrections" is about.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:46.886
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.720
What happened was,

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:53.726
I sort of played out in my head

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:56.061
what would go down

00:04:56.061 --> 00:04:59.898
if our security guys, Jim
and John, would have to escort

00:04:59.898 --> 00:05:01.934
a drunk gopher
out of the building.

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:05.738
And then I -- in my head,
I thought it would be funny

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:07.407
if Jim said, "Look out
for his teeth."

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:08.908
Now...

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:10.242
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:12.244
...why that became
really funny to me --

00:05:12.244 --> 00:05:15.914
and I'm trying not to let that
happen this minute --

00:05:15.914 --> 00:05:20.253
Jim and John are exceptional
security guards.

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:22.087
Exceptional.

00:05:22.087 --> 00:05:24.424
With that said...

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:27.426
that's not their best skill.

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:30.596
Their best skill is
busting each other's balls.

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:32.431
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.431 --> 00:05:36.769
And I know from history
that if a gopher bit John,

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:40.273
Jim would never let him
[bleep] forget about it.

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:43.776
Every day, I'd be walking
downstairs with them

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.277
and Jim would say, like,
"I'm gonna go out first,

00:05:45.277 --> 00:05:47.280
make sure there's no gophers
there for John."

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.114
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.114 --> 00:05:50.116
"John asked me to" --

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:51.784
[ Laughing ]

00:05:52.951 --> 00:05:55.288
"John wants me to go
check for gophers first."

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:56.956
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:59.125
And then John would --
John would love telling you.

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:01.294
If a gopher bit John...

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:03.296
"I'll tell you,
those teeth, Seth."

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:05.465
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:08.134
"Went right through my pant leg!

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:09.635
Two holes."

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:11.337
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.305 --> 00:06:15.308
"I told you to look out
for his teeth."

00:06:15.308 --> 00:06:18.311
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.311 --> 00:06:20.146
It's -- It is --
No, it is hot.

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:21.647
You don't think?

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:23.816
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:25.818
Oh, this was a nice comment.

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:27.153
"My wife hates you

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:28.654
and hates the 'Corrections' vids

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:31.490
even more than
your usual stuff."

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:34.326
All I will say is...

00:06:34.326 --> 00:06:36.329
she sounds like a keeper.

00:06:36.329 --> 00:06:38.297
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.333 --> 00:06:44.503
Uh, we referred to
an Italian fashion designer

00:06:44.503 --> 00:06:46.005
as Bruno Cucinelli.

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:47.006
That was incorrect.

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:48.507
His name is Bruno

00:06:48.507 --> 00:06:50.509
Cucinelli's monster.

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:53.012
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:54.380
[ Chuckles ]

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.450
Brunello.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:01.453
And this is one where

00:07:01.453 --> 00:07:02.788
everybody in the r--

00:07:02.788 --> 00:07:05.791
So, Emily,
our "Closer Look" producer,

00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:07.626
who is really
on these sort of things

00:07:07.626 --> 00:07:10.629
and is certainly,
on the surface,

00:07:10.629 --> 00:07:11.797
the most fashionable

00:07:11.797 --> 00:07:14.299
of everybody who works
in that room --

00:07:14.299 --> 00:07:15.635
this was one
she should've caught.

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:16.969
And I think she feels terrible
about it.

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:18.471
We're not gonna beat her up
on it, but, like,

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:21.140
you can't ask,
like, Shoemaker...

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.809
When you ask Shoemaker about,
like, luxury shoe designers,

00:07:23.809 --> 00:07:25.478
he's like, "Florsheim."

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:27.479
[ Laughter ]

00:07:27.479 --> 00:07:30.315
"I got one sayin' about shoes.

00:07:30.315 --> 00:07:32.652
The ceiling is Florsheim."

00:07:32.652 --> 00:07:33.986
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.986 --> 00:07:36.255
And then Sal has to pretend
like he doesn't know

00:07:36.255 --> 00:07:38.958
'cause he's secret rich and he
doesn't want, like, you know...

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.459
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.459 --> 00:07:43.462
Oh, my God, the hoops
that Sal goes through

00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:44.964
to be secret rich is so...

00:07:44.964 --> 00:07:46.465
I mean, we all have to,
like, pretend like,

00:07:46.465 --> 00:07:49.635
"Oh, here comes Sal in his
Mets hat and New Balance shoes."

00:07:49.635 --> 00:07:51.637
[ Laughter ]
But he's got, like --

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:54.473
Like, he's got this Gristedes
bag he carries around with him

00:07:54.473 --> 00:07:56.709
and then, like, you look and
it's, like, Ferragamo shoes,

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:58.478
Omega watch.

00:08:02.014 --> 00:08:03.516
Um, we said Obama --

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:07.019
if Obama was at the top
of Mount Everest,

00:08:07.019 --> 00:08:11.023
he would be wearing shades
and smoking a cigarette.

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:14.693
Here's the photo Graphics made.

00:08:14.693 --> 00:08:16.195
Now, you might note,

00:08:16.195 --> 00:08:20.700
the weird thing about being
at the top of Mount Everest

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:24.036
would be the big ol' mountain
behind it

00:08:24.036 --> 00:08:25.871
that's taller.

00:08:25.871 --> 00:08:28.874
[ Laughter ]

00:08:28.874 --> 00:08:30.209
[ Sniffs ]

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:32.711
Um...

00:08:32.711 --> 00:08:36.382
We said, um...

00:08:36.382 --> 00:08:39.719
Scollins made a joke
about, uh...

00:08:39.719 --> 00:08:41.387
There was a -- someone
broke a world record

00:08:41.387 --> 00:08:43.222
by making the world's largest
sushi roll --

00:08:43.222 --> 00:08:44.890
sushi roll, excuse me --

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:46.558
and then we said,
"Now the bad news,"

00:08:46.558 --> 00:08:48.894
and showed a picture of Shamu.

00:08:48.894 --> 00:08:50.896
Orcas are mammals,
so they wouldn't be good --

00:08:50.896 --> 00:08:51.897
this is what you guys told me.

00:08:51.897 --> 00:08:54.233
They wouldn't be good for sushi.

00:08:54.233 --> 00:08:57.903
They'd be good for,
like, a tartare.

00:08:57.903 --> 00:09:01.740
Also, Shamu died in the '70s.

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:03.241
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:03.241 --> 00:09:04.910
Jonestown.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:06.946
[ Laughter ]

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:13.252
So hot.

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:14.920
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:16.254
Maybe the gopher, like...

00:09:16.254 --> 00:09:19.925
Could the gopher have, like,
chewed through the cord

00:09:19.925 --> 00:09:21.761
to the AC?

00:09:21.761 --> 00:09:23.095
[ Laughter ]

00:09:23.095 --> 00:09:24.964
I mean, I don't think I'm crazy.

00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:28.935
Do you think I'm crazy?

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:31.404
Ahh.

00:09:31.404 --> 00:09:33.439
[ Laughter ]

00:09:39.911 --> 00:09:41.948
[ Laughter continues ]

00:09:45.584 --> 00:09:47.420
What else, what else?

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:49.288
[ Laughter ]

00:09:53.425 --> 00:09:54.593
Oh, I know why I'm hot.

00:09:54.593 --> 00:09:56.429
I did 50 push-ups.

00:09:56.429 --> 00:09:58.898
[ Laughter ]

